<title>ITALY: Italian futures closing report.</title>
<headline>Italian futures closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian bond futures ended a thin short day ahead of the Christmas holiday with prices under pressure from the on-going dispute between Italian metalworkers and employers, dealers said.</p>
<p>They added it was largely a session of booksquaring with a lack of buyers in the market, and with little clear direction to trade seen until into the start of the New Year.</p>
<p>The lack of an accord in the metalworkers' pay dispute looked likely to delay a long-awaited cut in the Bank of Italy's key interest rate, traders said.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
